- 'POs created before 2015' / 'purchase orders created since March 2024' -> target_entity 'PurchaseOrder' with a 'created_before' or 'created_since' filter whose value is an ISO date 'YYYY-MM-DD'. A date bound satisfies the PurchaseOrder root requirement, so no PO id is needed. Use ONLY when the question names an ABSOLUTE date or year. If it says something RELATIVE — 'older than 6 months', 'stale', 'in the last year', 'created in the last N months', 'created within the past N months' — set a 'created_in_last_n_months' filter with value {"months": N}. The planner computes the ISO cutoff from N and forwards it as 'created_before'; do NOT compute the date yourself and do NOT emit 'created_before' directly for a relative phrase.
